    * 🔗[Good Machine Learning Practice for Medical Device Development: Guiding Principles](https://www.fda.gov/medical-devices/software-medical-device-samd/good-machine-learning-practice-medical-device-development-guiding-principles) 
* **WHO Guidance on Ethics and Governance of AI for Health (2021):** Highlights responsibility, inclusiveness, safety, equity, and accountability, especially in global and low-resource contexts. 
    * 🔗 [WHO Guidance on Ethics and Governance of AI for Health](https://www.who.int/publications/i/item/9789240029200?utm_source=chatgpt.com) 
* **EU High-Level Expert Group on AI – Ethics Guidelines for Trustworthy AI (2019):** Sets out requirements including human agency, technical robustness, privacy, transparency, fairness, societal well-being, and accountability. 
    * 🔗 [EU Trustworthy AI Guidelines](https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/library/ethics-guidelines-trustworthy-ai)
* **OECD Principles on AI (2019):** Adopted globally, stressing inclusive growth, human-centered values, transparency, robustness, and accountability. 
